{
  "source": "REQUIREMENTS.md",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "text": "Streak is a mobile habit tracker (iOS and Android clients) where a user creates habits with a target count per week, month or year, checks in (also offline), sees whether the target is still reachable at the current rate, and gets nudges in the app and as push notifications. This document specifies the backend API: Go with Gin + GORM on MySQL.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements",
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "text": "The owner's idea did not state these; each is restated as a rule below. Review them first.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Assumptions made on the owner's behalf",
      "line": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "text": "Every route is under `/v1`, except `GET /health`, which answers 200 without a token.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Errors and versioning",
      "line": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "text": "Every error answers `{\"error\": {\"code\": <code>, \"message\": <text>}}`, plus `\"field\": <request field name>` when one request field caused it; `code` is one of the codes named in this document and never changes meaning.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Errors and versioning",
      "line": 76
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "text": "Every request body or query value that fails validation answers 422 with code `validation_failed` and the offending `field`, and writes nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Errors and versioning",
      "line": 77
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "text": "A request may send `X-Client-Version: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`; when it is lower than the configured minimum (`HABIT_MIN_CLIENT_VERSION`) or malformed, the request answers 426 with code `upgrade_required` and writes nothing; a request without the header is served.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Errors and versioning",
      "line": 78
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "text": "A refused or invalid request (any 4xx) writes nothing, with one exception: a 401 `refresh_token_reused` revokes every refresh token of that user and installation.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Errors and versioning",
      "line": 79
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "text": "`POST /v1/auth/register` takes `{email, password, timezone?}` and answers 201 `{id, email, timezone}`; the email is stored lower-cased and `timezone` defaults to `\"UTC\"`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 83
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "text": "A password is 8 to 72 bytes, an email must be valid, and a timezone must be an IANA zone name (e.g. `Europe/Berlin`); anything else answers 422 `validation_failed` and creates no user.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 84
    },
    {
      "id": "R10",
      "text": "An email already registered, compared case-insensitively, answers 409 with code `email_taken` and creates no user.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 85
    },
    {
      "id": "R11",
      "text": "Registering a user also creates their `notification_prefs` row with `push_enabled` true, `quiet_start` `\"22:00\"`, `quiet_end` `\"08:00\"` and `nudge_time` `\"20:00\"`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 86
    },
    {
      "id": "R12",
      "text": "The password is stored only as a bcrypt hash in `users.hashed_password`; no response ever contains the password, its hash, or a refresh token's hash.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 87
    },
    {
      "id": "R13",
      "text": "`POST /v1/auth/login` takes `{email, password, installation_id}` (`installation_id` a UUID the app generates once per install) and answers 200 `{access_token, refresh_token, token_type: \"bearer\", expires_in: 900}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 88
    },
    {
      "id": "R14",
      "text": "A wrong password or an unknown email at login answers 401 with code `invalid_credentials`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 89
    },
    {
      "id": "R15",
      "text": "The access token is a JWT signed HS256 with `HABIT_SECRET_KEY`, with `sub` = the user id and `sid` = the installation_id, expiring 15 minutes after it was issued by the app's clock.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "R16",
      "text": "The refresh token is an opaque random string of at least 32 bytes of entropy, valid for 30 days; the app stores only its SHA-256 hex digest in `refresh_tokens.token_hash`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 91
    },
    {
      "id": "R17",
      "text": "A user has at most one live refresh token per installation: a login revokes (sets `revoked_at` on) every unrevoked refresh token of the same user and installation before writing the new one.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 92
    },
    {
      "id": "R18",
      "text": "`POST /v1/auth/refresh` takes `{refresh_token}`; for a live token (not rotated, not revoked, not expired) it sets that token's `rotated_at`, writes a new refresh token for the same user and installation, and answers 200 with a new access token and the new refresh token in the login's shape.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 93
    },
    {
      "id": "R19",
      "text": "A refresh token that is unknown, expired or revoked answers 401 with code `invalid_refresh_token`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 94
    },
    {
      "id": "R20",
      "text": "A refresh token that was already rotated (reuse) answers 401 with code `refresh_token_reused` and revokes every refresh token of that user and installation, so the session must log in again.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 95
    },
    {
      "id": "R21",
      "text": "Every other `/v1` route except register, login and refresh needs `Authorization: Bearer <access token>`; without one it answers 401 with code `not_authenticated`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 96
    },
    {
      "id": "R22",
      "text": "An access token that is past its expiry answers 401 with code `token_expired`; a malformed or wrongly signed one, or one whose user no longer exists, answers 401 with code `invalid_token`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 97
    },
    {
      "id": "R23",
      "text": "`POST /v1/auth/logout` (signed in) revokes every refresh token of the caller's installation (the token's `sid`), deletes the caller's device row with that installation_id if any, and answers 204.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 98
    },
    {
      "id": "R24",
      "text": "`GET /v1/me` answers `{id, email, timezone, notification_prefs: {push_enabled, quiet_start, quiet_end, nudge_time}}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 99
    },
    {
      "id": "R25",
      "text": "`PUT /v1/me` takes any subset of `{timezone, push_enabled, quiet_start, quiet_end, nudge_time}` and answers 200 with the new `GET /v1/me` body; times are `\"HH:MM\"` 24-hour local times and an invalid value answers 422 `validation_failed` with nothing changed.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "R26",
      "text": "`DELETE /v1/me` answers 204 and permanently deletes the user with their notification prefs, devices, refresh tokens, habits, habit targets, check-ins and nudges (no tombstones); afterwards the user's old access token answers 401 `invalid_token` and their login answers 401 `invalid_credentials`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 101
    },
    {
      "id": "R27",
      "text": "There are no roles or admins: a user sees and changes only their own habits, check-ins, nudges and devices.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 102
    },
    {
      "id": "R28",
      "text": "A habit, check-in, nudge or device of another user answers 404 with code `not_found` on every route, exactly like an id that does not exist, and writes nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Accounts, tokens and sessions",
      "line": 103
    },
    {
      "id": "R29",
      "text": "A signed-in user may make 120 requests per clock minute (fixed windows starting at second 0); the 121st and later requests in that minute answer 429 with code `rate_limited` and a `Retry-After` header giving the seconds until the window ends, and write nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Rate limiting",
      "line": 107
    },
    {
      "id": "R30",
      "text": "A sync or batch request counts as one request whatever it contains.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Rate limiting",
      "line": 108
    },
    {
      "id": "R31",
      "text": "`POST /v1/devices` takes `{installation_id, platform, push_token, timezone, app_version}` and answers 201 with the device `{id, installation_id, platform, push_token, timezone, app_version}`; `platform` is `ios` or `android`, `push_token` 1 to 4096 characters, `timezone` an IANA zone, and anything else answers 422 `validation_failed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Devices and notification preferences",
      "line": 112
    },
    {
      "id": "R32",
      "text": "`POST /v1/devices` with a `push_token` that is already registered updates that device row's other fields, makes it the caller's, and answers 200 with it; there is never more than one row per `push_token`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Devices and notification preferences",
      "line": 113
    },
    {
      "id": "R33",
      "text": "`DELETE /v1/devices/{id}` answers 204 and deletes the caller's device row.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Devices and notification preferences",
      "line": 114
    },
    {
      "id": "R34",
      "text": "A device's `timezone` is stored for information only; it never changes the user's timezone.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Devices and notification preferences",
      "line": 115
    },
    {
      "id": "R35",
      "text": "`users`: `id` (integer), `email` (unique), `hashed_password`, `timezone`, `change_seq` (integer, the last change counter value given out, starting at 0), `created_at`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 119
    },
    {
      "id": "R36",
      "text": "`notification_prefs`: `user_id` (unique), `push_enabled`, `quiet_start`, `quiet_end`, `nudge_time` (all three `\"HH:MM\"`), `last_pass_date` (a date, nullable: the local date of the user's last daily pass).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "R37",
      "text": "`devices`: `id` (integer), `user_id`, `installation_id`, `platform` (`ios` | `android`), `push_token` (unique), `timezone`, `app_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 121
    },
    {
      "id": "R38",
      "text": "`refresh_tokens`: `id` (integer), `user_id`, `installation_id`, `token_hash` (unique), `expires_at`, `rotated_at` (nullable), `revoked_at` (nullable), `created_at`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 122
    },
    {
      "id": "R39",
      "text": "`habits`: `id` (a client UUID), `user_id`, `name`, `description` (nullable), `target_count`, `period` (`week` | `month` | `year`), `start_date`, `end_date` (nullable), `archived` (default false), `version` (starts at 1), `change_seq`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at` (nullable).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 123
    },
    {
      "id": "R40",
      "text": "`habit_targets`: `id` (integer), `habit_id`, `target_count`, `effective_from` (the first day of the period from which this target applies); one row per (`habit_id`, `effective_from`).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 124
    },
    {
      "id": "R41",
      "text": "`completions`: `id` (a client UUID), `habit_id`, `date` (the user's local date), `note` (nullable), `change_seq`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at` (nullable); at most one non-deleted row per (`habit_id`, `date`).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 125
    },
    {
      "id": "R42",
      "text": "`nudges`: `id` (a server UUID), `habit_id`, `for_date` (a local date), `kind` (`on_track` | `behind` | `unreachable` | `achieved`), `message`, `delivery` (`pending` | `sent` | `failed` | `suppressed`), `delivery_reason` (nullable: `quiet_hours` | `push_disabled` | `no_device` | `daily_limit` | `in_app_only` | `after_daily_pass` | `dismissed`), `change_seq`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `dismissed_at` (nullable), `deleted_at` (nullable); one row per (`habit_id`, `for_date`).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 126
    },
    {
      "id": "R43",
      "text": "Dates travel as `YYYY-MM-DD` strings and instants as ISO-8601 UTC strings ending in `Z`; every stored instant is UTC; a malformed date or id in a request answers 422 `validation_failed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Data model (table and column names are fixed)",
      "line": 127
    },
    {
      "id": "R44",
      "text": "The app reads the current instant only from its clock: the real time in production, and in test mode the instant the harness sets (see CONTEXT.md).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Time, timezones and periods",
      "line": 131
    },
    {
      "id": "R45",
      "text": "A user's \"today\" (written `t` below) is the calendar date of the current instant in the user's `timezone`; every day and period boundary is computed in that timezone.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Time, timezones and periods",
      "line": 132
    },
    {
      "id": "R46",
      "text": "A weekly period runs Monday to Sunday, a monthly period from the 1st to the last day of the calendar month, a yearly period from January 1 to December 31, all as local dates; `L` is the number of days in the period (7; 28 to 31; 365 or 366).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Time, timezones and periods",
      "line": 133
    },
    {
      "id": "R47",
      "text": "Changing the user's timezone changes only what today is from then on: check-ins keep the local `date` they were made with, and no period or past check-in is recomputed.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Time, timezones and periods",
      "line": 134
    },
    {
      "id": "R48",
      "text": "A habit's target applies again in every period, from the period containing `start_date` until the period containing `end_date` (or for ever when `end_date` is null); archiving does not change the periods, it only stops nudges and check-ins.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Time, timezones and periods",
      "line": 135
    },
    {
      "id": "R49",
      "text": "`POST /v1/habits` takes `{id, name, description?, target_count, period, start_date?, end_date?}` (`id` a UUID the client generated) and answers 201 with the habit `{id, name, description, target_count, period, start_date, end_date, archived, version, created_at, updated_at}`; `archived` is false and `version` is 1.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 139
    },
    {
      "id": "R50",
      "text": "`start_date` defaults to the user's today; it may be in the past or the future.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "R51",
      "text": "`name` is 1 to 100 characters and not only whitespace, `description` at most 500 characters, `period` one of `week`, `month`, `year`, and `target_count` an integer from 1 to 7 for `week`, 31 for `month` and 366 for `year`; anything else answers 422 `validation_failed` with that `field`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 141
    },
    {
      "id": "R52",
      "text": "`end_date`, when given, must be on or after `start_date`; an earlier one answers 422 `validation_failed` with field `end_date`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 142
    },
    {
      "id": "R53",
      "text": "`POST /v1/habits` with the id of an existing habit of the caller whose name, description, target_count, period, start_date and end_date all equal the request's answers 200 with the existing habit and writes nothing (a retried create).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 143
    },
    {
      "id": "R54",
      "text": "`POST /v1/habits` with an id that exists with different content, belongs to another user, or belongs to a deleted habit answers 409 with code `id_conflict` and writes nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 144
    },
    {
      "id": "R55",
      "text": "A habit name is unique among the user's non-deleted habits, archived or not, compared case-insensitively (`Run` and `run` conflict); a duplicate on create or on rename answers 409 with code `name_taken`. Another user may use the same name.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 145
    },
    {
      "id": "R56",
      "text": "A user has at most 50 active (non-archived, non-deleted) habits; creating one more answers 409 with code `habit_limit`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 146
    },
    {
      "id": "R57",
      "text": "Creating a habit also writes its first `habit_targets` row: its `target_count`, with `effective_from` = the first day of the period containing `start_date`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 147
    },
    {
      "id": "R58",
      "text": "`GET /v1/habits` answers `{items, next_cursor, has_more}` with the caller's non-deleted, non-archived habits ordered by id; `?include_archived=true` includes archived ones.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 148
    },
    {
      "id": "R59",
      "text": "`GET /v1/habits/{id}` answers the habit; a deleted habit answers 404 `not_found`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 149
    },
    {
      "id": "R60",
      "text": "`PATCH /v1/habits/{id}` takes `{version, ...}` with any subset of `{name, description, target_count, start_date, end_date, archived}` and answers 200 with the updated habit, its `version` one higher; the same validation as creation applies.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 150
    },
    {
      "id": "R61",
      "text": "A `PATCH` without `version` answers 422 `validation_failed` with field `version`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 151
    },
    {
      "id": "R62",
      "text": "A `PATCH` whose `version` is not the habit's current version answers 409 `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"version_conflict\", ...}, \"current\": <the habit as stored>}` and changes nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 152
    },
    {
      "id": "R63",
      "text": "A `PATCH` body that contains `period` answers 422 `validation_failed` with field `period` and changes nothing.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 153
    },
    {
      "id": "R64",
      "text": "`description: null` and `end_date: null` in a `PATCH` clear them.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 154
    },
    {
      "id": "R65",
      "text": "Changing `target_count` updates `habits.target_count` and writes the `habit_targets` row for the current period (`effective_from` = the first day of the period containing today, or of the period containing `start_date` when the habit has not started yet), replacing that row's value if it exists; rows of earlier periods never change.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 155
    },
    {
      "id": "R66",
      "text": "The new `target_count` applies to the current period at once: progress and nudges use it from the next request on.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 156
    },
    {
      "id": "R67",
      "text": "`start_date` can be changed only while today is before the current `start_date`; otherwise the change answers 409 with code `start_date_locked`. A permitted change moves the habit's only `habit_targets` row to the period containing the new `start_date`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 157
    },
    {
      "id": "R68",
      "text": "`end_date` can be changed at any time, also to a past date (which ends the habit); an `end_date` before the date of one of the habit's non-deleted check-ins answers 409 with code `checkins_after_end`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 158
    },
    {
      "id": "R69",
      "text": "`archived: true` archives the habit and `archived: false` restores it; restoring when the user already has 50 active habits answers 409 `habit_limit`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 159
    },
    {
      "id": "R70",
      "text": "`DELETE /v1/habits/{id}` answers 204, sets the habit's `deleted_at`, increments its `version`, and sets `deleted_at` on its non-deleted check-ins and nudges; nothing is removed from the database.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 160
    },
    {
      "id": "R71",
      "text": "Every change to a habit, check-in or nudge (create, update, soft delete, dismissal, a nudge rewrite) increments the owner's `users.change_seq` and stores the new value in that row's `change_seq`, and sets its `updated_at` to now.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Habits",
      "line": 161
    },
    {
      "id": "R72",
      "text": "`POST /v1/habits/{habit_id}/completions` takes `{id, date, note?}` (`id` a client UUID, `date` the user's local date) and answers 201 `{id, habit_id, date, note, created_at, updated_at}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 165
    },
    {
      "id": "R73",
      "text": "A check-in `date` after the user's today answers 422 with code `date_in_future`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 166
    },
    {
      "id": "R74",
      "text": "A check-in `date` before the habit's `start_date` or after its `end_date` answers 422 with code `date_out_of_range`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 167
    },
    {
      "id": "R75",
      "text": "A check-in `date` more than 60 days before the user's today (earlier than `t - 60`) answers 422 with code `date_too_old`; `t - 60` itself is accepted.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 168
    },
    {
      "id": "R76",
      "text": "When several of these date rules apply at once, the code answered is `date_in_future` first, then `date_out_of_range`, then `date_too_old`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 169
    },
    {
      "id": "R77",
      "text": "`note` is at most 280 characters; longer answers 422 `validation_failed` with field `note`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 170
    },
    {
      "id": "R78",
      "text": "A habit has at most one non-deleted check-in per date; another one with a new id answers 409 with code `already_checked_in`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 171
    },
    {
      "id": "R79",
      "text": "A check-in with the id of an existing check-in of the same habit, date and note answers 200 with the existing one and writes nothing; the same id with different content, under another habit, or of a deleted check-in answers 409 `id_conflict`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 172
    },
    {
      "id": "R80",
      "text": "Creating or deleting a check-in on an archived habit answers 409 with code `habit_archived`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 173
    },
    {
      "id": "R81",
      "text": "`GET /v1/habits/{habit_id}/completions` answers `{items, next_cursor, has_more}` with the habit's non-deleted check-ins ordered by date ascending; `?from=` and `?to=` (local dates, inclusive) filter by date, and `from` after `to` answers 422 `validation_failed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 174
    },
    {
      "id": "R82",
      "text": "`DELETE /v1/habits/{habit_id}/completions/{id}` answers 204 and sets the check-in's `deleted_at`; a check-in of a different habit, or one already deleted, answers 404 `not_found`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 175
    },
    {
      "id": "R83",
      "text": "`POST /v1/completions/batch` takes `{items: [{id, habit_id, date, note?}, ...]}` with 1 to 100 items, else 422 `validation_failed` with field `items`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 176
    },
    {
      "id": "R84",
      "text": "A batch processes its items in order, each exactly as a single check-in create would, and answers 200 `{results: [{id, status, code?, completion?}, ...]}` in the items' order, where `status` is `created` (with the completion), `existing` (an identical retry, with the completion) or `rejected` (with the `code` the single create would answer, e.g. `not_found`, `date_too_old`, `already_checked_in`, `id_conflict`).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 177
    },
    {
      "id": "R85",
      "text": "A batch item that is rejected writes nothing, and never stops the other items.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Check-ins",
      "line": 178
    },
    {
      "id": "R86",
      "text": "A list answers `{items, next_cursor, has_more}`; `?limit=` is 1 to 200 (default 50), any other value answers 422 `validation_failed`, and `?cursor=` is the `next_cursor` of the previous page.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Lists and pagination",
      "line": 182
    },
    {
      "id": "R87",
      "text": "`has_more` is true exactly when more items follow; `next_cursor` is null when `has_more` is false.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Lists and pagination",
      "line": 183
    },
    {
      "id": "R88",
      "text": "A cursor that the app did not issue answers 422 with code `invalid_cursor`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Lists and pagination",
      "line": 184
    },
    {
      "id": "R89",
      "text": "`GET /v1/sync?cursor=<opaque>&limit=<n>` answers `{changes, next_cursor, has_more}`: the caller's habits, check-ins and nudges whose `change_seq` is greater than the cursor's, ordered by `change_seq` ascending.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 188
    },
    {
      "id": "R90",
      "text": "Each change is `{type: \"habit\" | \"completion\" | \"nudge\", id, change_seq, deleted, data}`, where `deleted` is true for a soft-deleted row (a tombstone) and `data` is the row in its normal response shape (null for a tombstone).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 189
    },
    {
      "id": "R91",
      "text": "A missing or empty cursor means a full sync: every change from the start, tombstones included.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 190
    },
    {
      "id": "R92",
      "text": "`limit` is 1 to 200 (default 100); any other value answers 422 `validation_failed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 191
    },
    {
      "id": "R93",
      "text": "`next_cursor` is always present and encodes the `change_seq` of the last change returned (or the request's own cursor position when nothing is returned); `has_more` is true exactly when more changes follow.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 192
    },
    {
      "id": "R94",
      "text": "A cursor that the app did not issue answers 422 with code `invalid_cursor`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Sync",
      "line": 193
    },
    {
      "id": "R95",
      "text": "`GET /v1/habits/{id}/progress` answers 200 `{habit_id, period, period_start, period_end, target, done, days_elapsed, days_remaining, rate_per_day, rate_per_period, required_per_day, required_per_period, projected, status}`, computed exactly by the rules of this section, all dates being local dates of the user.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 197
    },
    {
      "id": "R96",
      "text": "The current period is the period containing `t` (the user's today); `period_start` and `period_end` are its first and last day.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 198
    },
    {
      "id": "R97",
      "text": "The active window is `as = max(period_start, start_date)` to `ae = min(period_end, end_date)` (`ae = period_end` when `end_date` is null), and `A = ae - as + 1` is its number of days.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 199
    },
    {
      "id": "R98",
      "text": "`N` is the habit's current `target_count`; the effective target is `target = N` when `A = L`, else `target = (N*A + L - 1) div L` (pro-rated and rounded up; `div` is integer division throughout).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 200
    },
    {
      "id": "R99",
      "text": "`done` = `D` is the number of the habit's non-deleted check-ins dated from `as` to `ae` inclusive.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 201
    },
    {
      "id": "R100",
      "text": "`days_elapsed` = `E = t - as + 1` (today included) and `days_remaining` = `R = ae - t` (days after today).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 202
    },
    {
      "id": "R101",
      "text": "`open_today` is 1 when the habit has no non-deleted check-in dated `t`, else 0; the capacity `C = R + open_today` is the most check-ins still possible in the period, and `needed = max(0, target - D)`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 203
    },
    {
      "id": "R102",
      "text": "`projected = (D*A) div E`, the total at the current rate.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 204
    },
    {
      "id": "R103",
      "text": "A rate `x / y` is reported in hundredths, rounded half up: `h(x, y) = (200*x + y) div (2*y)`, answered as the JSON number `h / 100` (e.g. 233 is answered as 2.33).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 205
    },
    {
      "id": "R104",
      "text": "`rate_per_day = h(D, E)` and `rate_per_period = h(D*L, E)` (the current rate scaled to a whole period).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 206
    },
    {
      "id": "R105",
      "text": "`required_per_day = h(needed, C)` and `required_per_period = h(needed*L, C)` when `C > 0` and `needed > 0`; both are 0 when `needed = 0`, and both are null when `needed > 0` and `C = 0`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 207
    },
    {
      "id": "R106",
      "text": "`status` is the first that applies: `not_started` if `t < start_date`; `achieved` if `D >= target`; `unreachable` if `needed > C`; `on_track` if `projected >= target`, or if `E = 1` and `D = 0` (the first day of the active window); `behind` otherwise.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 208
    },
    {
      "id": "R107",
      "text": "A habit that has not started (`t < start_date`) answers the period containing `start_date`, with `D = 0`, `days_elapsed = 0`, `days_remaining = A`, `C = A`, both current rates 0, `projected = 0`, the required rates `h(target, A)` and `h(target*L, A)`, and `status = \"not_started\"`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 209
    },
    {
      "id": "R108",
      "text": "A habit whose `end_date` is before today answers the period containing `end_date`, computed as if `t = end_date` with `open_today = 0` (so `days_remaining = 0`, `C = 0`), and its status is `achieved` or `unreachable`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 210
    },
    {
      "id": "R109",
      "text": "Example (user in America/New_York, clock 2026-03-04T12:00:00Z, so today is Wednesday 2026-03-04): a weekly habit with target 3 started 2026-03-02 with one check-in dated 2026-03-02 answers `period_start` 2026-03-02, `period_end` 2026-03-08, `target` 3, `done` 1, `days_elapsed` 3, `days_remaining` 4, `rate_per_day` 0.33, `rate_per_period` 2.33, `required_per_day` 0.4, `required_per_period` 2.8, `projected` 2, `status` `behind`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 211
    },
    {
      "id": "R110",
      "text": "Example (same user and clock): a weekly habit with target 4 starting 2026-03-04 has `target` 3 (5 active days of 7: `(4*5 + 6) div 7`), `done` 0, `days_elapsed` 1 and `status` `on_track`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 212
    },
    {
      "id": "R111",
      "text": "Example (same user and clock): a weekly habit with target 6 started 2026-03-02 with no check-ins has `needed` 6 > `C` 5, so `status` is `unreachable`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 213
    },
    {
      "id": "R112",
      "text": "Example (same user and clock): a monthly habit with target 10 started 2026-03-01 with check-ins dated March 1, 2 and 3 has `target` 10, `done` 3, `days_elapsed` 4, `days_remaining` 27, `projected` 23 and `status` `on_track`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 214
    },
    {
      "id": "R113",
      "text": "Example (timezone): at clock 2026-03-09T02:00:00Z it is still Sunday 2026-03-08 22:00 in America/New_York, so that user's current week is 2026-03-02 to 2026-03-08 with `days_remaining` 0, while for a user in UTC it is Monday 2026-03-09 and a new week.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Progress of the current period",
      "line": 215
    },
    {
      "id": "R114",
      "text": "`GET /v1/home` answers `{today, habits, nudges}`: `today` the user's local date; `habits` every non-deleted, non-archived habit of the caller ordered by id, each the habit's normal body plus `progress` equal to its `GET /v1/habits/{id}/progress` body; `nudges` the caller's active nudges as a plain array (not paginated), the same nudges `GET /v1/nudges` lists, ordered by `habit_id`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Home screen",
      "line": 219
    },
    {
      "id": "R115",
      "text": "A nudge is a habit's status for one local day, stored in `nudges` with `for_date` = that day, `kind` = the status, and `message` built exactly from the templates below; `not_started` gets no nudge.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 223
    },
    {
      "id": "R116",
      "text": "`on_track` message: `On track: {done} of {target} this {unit}. Keep it up!`, where `{unit}` is `week`, `month` or `year`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 224
    },
    {
      "id": "R117",
      "text": "`behind` message: `Behind: do {needed} more in the next {C} day(s). Needs {required_per_period} per {unit}, you are at {rate_per_period}.`, the rates written with exactly two decimals (e.g. `2.80`, `0.00`).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 225
    },
    {
      "id": "R118",
      "text": "`unreachable` message: `Out of reach this {unit}: at most {D + C} of {target}. A new {unit} starts on {period_end + 1 day}.`",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 226
    },
    {
      "id": "R119",
      "text": "`achieved` message: `Goal reached: {done} of {target} this {unit}. Nice work!`",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 227
    },
    {
      "id": "R120",
      "text": "Example: the first progress example's nudge is `Behind: do 2 more in the next 5 day(s). Needs 2.80 per week, you are at 2.33.`",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 228
    },
    {
      "id": "R121",
      "text": "No nudge is ever created or rewritten for a deleted or archived habit, a habit that has not started, or a habit whose `end_date` is before the user's today.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 229
    },
    {
      "id": "R122",
      "text": "Every check-in write that succeeds (a created or deleted check-in, also in a batch) computes the habit's status for the user's today and, for an eligible habit, creates today's nudge or rewrites the `kind` and `message` of today's existing nudge unless it is dismissed; the write's own answer is unchanged by this.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 230
    },
    {
      "id": "R123",
      "text": "Rewriting a nudge never changes its `delivery` or `delivery_reason`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 231
    },
    {
      "id": "R124",
      "text": "A nudge created by a check-in write before the user's daily pass of that day has `delivery` `pending`; one created after that day's pass has `delivery` `suppressed` with reason `after_daily_pass`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 232
    },
    {
      "id": "R125",
      "text": "A dismissed nudge is never rewritten, recreated or pushed for the same day.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 233
    },
    {
      "id": "R126",
      "text": "The background service `nudger` checks every minute (and once at start-up), for each user, whether the user's local time has reached their `nudge_time` and their `last_pass_date` is before their local today; if so it runs that user's daily pass and sets `last_pass_date` to the local today.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 234
    },
    {
      "id": "R127",
      "text": "A daily pass, for each eligible habit of the user in id order, creates today's nudge or rewrites its `kind` and `message` (unless dismissed), then decides the delivery of each of today's nudges that is still `pending`, in habit id order, by the first rule that applies.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 235
    },
    {
      "id": "R128",
      "text": "Delivery rule 1: a dismissed nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `dismissed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 236
    },
    {
      "id": "R129",
      "text": "Delivery rule 2: an `on_track` or `achieved` nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `in_app_only`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 237
    },
    {
      "id": "R130",
      "text": "Delivery rule 3: if the user's `push_enabled` is false, the nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `push_disabled`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 238
    },
    {
      "id": "R131",
      "text": "Delivery rule 4: if the user has no device row, the nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `no_device`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 239
    },
    {
      "id": "R132",
      "text": "Delivery rule 5: if the user's local time is inside their quiet hours (from `quiet_start` inclusive to `quiet_end` exclusive, crossing midnight when `quiet_start` is later than `quiet_end`; no quiet hours when they are equal), the nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `quiet_hours`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "R133",
      "text": "Delivery rule 6: if 3 of the user's nudges for that local day already have `delivery` `sent`, the nudge becomes `suppressed` with reason `daily_limit`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 241
    },
    {
      "id": "R134",
      "text": "Delivery rule 7: otherwise the push service sends the nudge's message to every device of the user; the nudge becomes `sent` if at least one send succeeded, else `failed` (reason null in both cases).",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 242
    },
    {
      "id": "R135",
      "text": "So a habit gets at most one push per day and a user at most 3 pushes per local day; every nudge, pushed or not, stays in the in-app list.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 243
    },
    {
      "id": "R136",
      "text": "Sending a push goes only through the push service interface (`PushSender`), which the test harness replaces with a stub.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 244
    },
    {
      "id": "R137",
      "text": "`GET /v1/nudges` answers `{items, next_cursor, has_more}` (default page 50, maximum 200, as every list) with the caller's active nudges ordered by `habit_id`: those with `for_date` = the user's today, `dismissed_at` and `deleted_at` null, and a non-archived habit; each item as `{id, habit_id, for_date, kind, message, delivery, delivery_reason, dismissed_at}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 245
    },
    {
      "id": "R138",
      "text": "`POST /v1/nudges/{id}/dismiss` sets `dismissed_at` to now and answers 200 with the nudge; a nudge already dismissed answers 409 with code `nudge_dismissed`, unchanged.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 246
    },
    {
      "id": "R139",
      "text": "A dismissal belongs to the user, not to a device: a dismissed nudge is not returned as active by `GET /v1/nudges`, by the `nudges` of `GET /v1/home` or by `GET /v1/sync` for any device or installation of that user, and `GET /v1/sync` returns the dismissed nudge as a `nudge` change with `deleted` false and `data.dismissed_at` set, so the user's other devices remove it locally.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 247
    },
    {
      "id": "R140",
      "text": "After a successful `POST /v1/nudges/{id}/dismiss`, the push service sends a silent clear push for that nudge (carrying the nudge's id) to every device of the user except the device row whose `installation_id` equals the caller's `sid`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 248
    },
    {
      "id": "R141",
      "text": "A clear push that fails does not fail the dismiss (it still answers 200) and does not change the nudge's `delivery` or `delivery_reason`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 249
    },
    {
      "id": "R142",
      "text": "A dismiss answered 409 `nudge_dismissed` sends no push.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 250
    },
    {
      "id": "R143",
      "text": "Clear pushes never count towards the daily limit of 3 pushes in delivery rule 6.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > Nudges",
      "line": 251
    },
    {
      "id": "R144",
      "text": "`GET /v1/habits/{id}/history` answers the habit's past periods, newest first, as `{items: [{period_start, period_end, target, done, achieved}]}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > History",
      "line": 255
    },
    {
      "id": "R145",
      "text": "A past period is one whose last day is before the user's today, from the period containing `start_date` up to the last period before the current one, and never after the period containing `end_date`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > History",
      "line": 256
    },
    {
      "id": "R146",
      "text": "A past period's `target` is the `target_count` of the habit's `habit_targets` row with the latest `effective_from` on or before that period's first day, pro-rated by the period's active window as in the progress rules; `done` is the number of non-deleted check-ins in its active window; `achieved` is `done >= target`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > History",
      "line": 257
    },
    {
      "id": "R147",
      "text": "`?limit=n` (1 to 100, default 12) answers at most n periods; any other limit answers 422 `validation_failed`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > History",
      "line": 258
    },
    {
      "id": "R148",
      "text": "A habit that has not started (today before `start_date`) answers 409 with code `habit_not_started`; a started habit with no past period answers 200 `{\"items\": []}`.",
      "section": "Streak: requirements > History",
      "line": 259
    }
  ],
